DiOPnn9gCzys</div><div data-ai-no-open-header="" data-content="1-142747">Learn more about H&amp;F Green Investment</div><div data-ai-no-open-words="" data-content="1-142748">The latest phase of H&amp;F Green Investment closed in June 2026. The council intends to launch more investments in the future, sign up for updates to get more news.</div><div data-ai-no-open-button-text="" data-content="1-142749">Signup for updates</div><div data-ai-no-open-button-url="" data-content="1-142750">/signup-for-updates</div><div data-ai-no-past-invest-header="" data-content="1-142751">Placeholder</div><div data-ai-no-past-invest-copy="" data-content="1-142752">placeholder</div><div data-ai-no-past-invest-button-url="" data-content="1-142753">/</div><div data-ai-no-past-invest-button-text="" data-content="1-142754">Learn more</div><div data-ai-no-chart-img-url="" data-content="1-142755">https://cdn4.sharein.com/abundance/cms/fd81e4f6-d21a-4e91-84fd-4b7e41b130f2.jpg</div><div data-ai-no-chart-img-alt="" data-content="1-142756">An image of a greening project</div><div data-ai-no-chart-img-caption="" data-content="2-142757">The council has been investing in greening projects across the borough</div></div><section class="position-relative bg-colour--primary-surface p-t-spacer-4xl type-white ai-hero" style="background:#e5f7e6"><div class="container"><div class="row brand-media-box align-items-start"><div class="col-12 col-md-8"><h1 class="text-choke-md--640 text-center--md font-secondary" style="color:#4c4c4a" data-content="1-142758">Hammersmith &amp; Fulham Council</h1><p class="body--xl text-choke-md--640 text-center--md m-b-spacer-sm" style="color:#4c4c4a" data-content="2-142762">Hammersmith &amp; Fulham Council is working to make their local area cleaner and greener to support people and nature</p></div><div class="col-12 col-md-4"><div class="ai-heroLogoRail"><img class="image-responsive hero-header__illustration brand-media-box__img" src="https://cdn4.sharein.com/abundance/cms/9032e3f9-6bee-4069-bb9d-695d9cbfb794.png" alt="Hammersmith &amp; Fulham Council logo" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high"></div></div></div></div></section><div class="bg-colour--primary-surface bg-mask bg-mask--b-convex m-b-spacer-2xl ai-hero-mask" style="background:#e5f7e6"></div><section class="m-b-spacer-md"><div class="container text-choke-960"><div class="row"><div class="col-12 text-center" data-content="2-142767"><p class="body--xl">Hammersmith &amp; Fulham Council is working to make their patch of London cleaner and greener. Its top-rated climate and ecological strategy and action plan - developed in collaboration with residents - guides their ambitious journey to making H&amp;F carbon net zero.</p><div class="choke-840 w-100 mx-auto m-y-spacer-md" data-aspect="16-9"><iframe width="560" height="315" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/n3u5jmgtlhs?si=jP-39FYqFwLayQ45" title="YouTube video player" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen=""></iframe></div><p class="body--xl">The council aims to raise £5 million through a series of investments which will help fund a range of projects from their climate action programme. These will include projects that can cut carbon emissions, as well as improving the local environment and helping residents adapt to the impact of the changing climate on its urban borough.</p><p class="body--xl text-center"></p><blockquote class="brand-blockquote"><p class="font-secondary">Hammersmith &amp; Fulham Council is at the forefront of the green finance revolution. Investors know that their money is being invested in projects that will make a positive impact on our communities, and people’s lives.<br><br> Meanwhile, it means that the council can deliver climate and ecological projects cost-effectively, which will help save taxpayer money. It’s a rare win-win-win.</p><footer class="choke-600 w-100 mx-auto"><img loading="lazy" src="https://cdn4.sharein.com/abundance/721452c5-0310-4766-847e-fbca0e347335.png" alt="Rowan Ree" title="Image: https://cdn4.sharein.com/abundance/721452c5-0310-4766-847e-fbca0e347335.png"><div><p>Cllr Rowan Ree</p><cite>Cabinet Member for Finance and Reform, Hammersmith &amp; Fulham Council</cite></div></footer></blockquote><p></p></div></div></div></section><div id="ai-scope-wrap"><div class="bg-colour--primary-surface bg-mask bg-mask--t-convex ai-no-open-mask ai-scope" style="background-color: rgb(255, 237, 204);"></div><section class="home-green-investing position-relative p-y-spacer-xs bg-colour--primary-surface ai-no-open ai-scope" style="background-color: rgb(255, 237, 204);"><div class="container"><div class="row"><div class="col-12"><div class="flex-center"><h2 class="text-center m-b-spacer-sm">Learn more about H&amp;F Green Investment</h2></div><div class="flex-center"><p class="body--lg text-center choke-800 m-b-spacer-sm">The latest phase of H&amp;F Green Investment closed in June 2026. The council intends to launch more investments in the future, sign up for updates to get more news.</p></div><div class="flex-center ai-no-open-btn-wrap"><a href="/signup-for-updates" class="brand-btn-grey--bordered brand-btn-grey--bordered--bordered btn btn--lg m-y-spacer-md btn--icon" style="border-color:#4c4c4a;color:#4c4c4a">Signup for updates</a></div></div></div></div></section><div class="bg-colour--primary-surface bg-mask bg-mask--b-convex ai-no-open-mask ai-scope" style="background-color: rgb(255, 237, 204);"></div><div class="bg-colour--primary-surface bg-mask bg-mask--t-convex ai-open-bg ai-scope" style="display: none;"></div><section class="home-green-investing position-relative p-y-spacer-xs ai-open-bg ai-scope" style="display: none;"><div class="container"><div class="row"><div class="col-12"><div class="flex-center"><h2 class="text-center m-b-spacer-sm" data-content="1-142759">Invest in H&amp;F Green Investment today</h2></div><div class="flex-center"><div class="ai-custom ai-open-investments"><div id="ai-open-councils"></div></div></div></div></div></div></section><div class="bg-colour--primary-surface bg-mask bg-mask--b-convex ai-open-bg ai-scope" style="display: none;"></div><section class="home-financial m-y-spacer-md p-y-spacer-xl mx-auto choke-800 ai-scope"><div class="container"><div class="row"><div class="col-12"><div class="flex-center"><h2 class="text-center" data-content="1-142760">How the council is spending the money</h2></div><div class="flex-center"><p class="body--lg text-center choke-800 m-b-spacer-lg"><span data-content="2-142769">Nearly <b>£500,000 has been fully spent</b> on completed green projects across the borough, and<span>&nbsp;approximately <b>£2.4 million’s worth of green projects are currently in delivery</b> – from design and consultation through to construction on the ground.<br><br><span>Completed projects include <a href="https://www.lbhf.gov.uk/news/2025/01/rain-gardens-create-green-shield-fight-flooding" target="_blank" rel="noopener" title="Link: https://www.lbhf.gov.uk/news/2025/01/rain-gardens-create-green-shield-fight-flooding">new award-winning rain gardens</a>&nbsp;at&nbsp;</span>King Street in Hammersmith, creating natural flood defences while enhancing the street scene for local businesses and residents.&nbsp;Similar schemes are blooming in Edith Road, West Kensington, and&nbsp;Purscell Crescent in Fulham.&nbsp;Meanwhile at Westville Road in Shepherds Bush,&nbsp;<span>old tarmac is making way for sustainable drainage, trees and new paths, bringing a biodiversity boost to the new and improved park area.<br></span><br><span>These projects join other success stories like&nbsp;the transformation from concrete paddling pool to <a href="https://www.lbhf.gov.uk/news/2024/04/volunteers-sow-seeds-change-eelbrook-common" target="_blank" rel="noopener">green sanctuary at Eelbrook Common</a> and a new <a href="https://www.lbhf.gov.uk/news/2024/08/frank-banfield-parks-new-ps400000-community-garden" target="_blank" rel="noopener" title="Link: https://www.lbhf.gov.uk/news/2024/08/frank-banfield-parks-new-ps400000-community-garden">community garden in Frank Banfield Park</a> – all funded with money raised from H&amp;F Green Investment.</span></span></span></p></div><div class="flex-center ai-uof-wrap"><div id="ai-use-of-funds"><div id="council-bar-chart"><div class="cbc-card"><section class="cbc-summary" id="cbc-summary" aria-live="polite"><div class="cbc-summary-inner"><div class="cbc-summary-logo"><a class="cbc-summary-logo-link" href="https://www.abundanceinvestment.com/council/hammersmith-and-fulham" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><div class="cbc-logo-badge" style="background:#e5f7e6;"><img src="https://cdn4.sharein.com/abundance/cms/eb6a2afb-89ad-4fee-9e3a-15f66107a8a3.png" alt="Hammersmith &amp; Fulham Council logo"></div></a></div><div class="cbc-summary-lines" role="list"><div class="cbc-summary-line" role="listitem">6 investments</div><div class="cbc-summary-line" role="listitem">£480k spent</div><div class="cbc-summary-line" role="listitem">12 projects financed</div></div></div></section><div class="cbc-chart" id="cbc-chart"><div class="cbc-row"><div class="cbc-label">Climate change adaptation</div><div class="cbc-bar-wrapper"><div class="cbc-bar-fill" data-final-width="62.774622858481855" style="width: 62.7746%; background: rgb(177, 145, 203);"><span class="cbc-bar-value">62.8%</span></div></div></div><div class="cbc-row"><div class="cbc-label">Clean transportation</div><div class="cbc-bar-wrapper"><div class="cbc-bar-fill" data-final-width="20.851005429226497" style="width: 20.851%; background: rgb(241, 202, 141);"><span class="cbc-bar-value">20.9%</span></div></div></div><div class="cbc-row"><div class="cbc-label">Living and natural resources</div><div class="cbc-bar-wrapper"><div class="cbc-bar-fill" data-final-width="16.374371712291655" style="width: 16.3744%; background: rgb(33, 224, 244);"><span class="cbc-bar-value">16.4%</span></div></div></div></div><section class="cbc-projects"><h3 class="cbc-projects__title">Top projects financed</h3><div class="cbc-projects__list"><details class="cbc-proj"><summary class="cbc-proj__sum"><div class="cbc-proj__pill" style="background:#f1ca8d;color:#111827;border:1px solid rgba(17,24,39,.10);">Clean Transportation</div><div class="cbc-proj__titleRow"><h4 class="cbc-proj__name">Cycle Storage Hubs</h4><div class="cbc-proj__right"><span class="cbc-proj__spent">£100,000.00</span><svg class="cbc-proj__chev" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path fill="currentColor" d="M5.3 7.3a1 1 0 0 1 1.4 0L10 10.6l3.3-3.3a1 1 0 1 1 1.4 1.4l-4 4a1 1 0 0 1-1.4 0l-4-4a1 1 0 0 1 0-1.4z"></path></svg></div></div></summary><div class="cbc-proj__body"><p>Cycle storage hubs installed to provide safe and secure bike shelters, with tool stations for quick fixes and flat tires. This will help tackle lack of storage space as a significant barrier to active travel in the borough.</p></div></details><details class="cbc-proj"><summary class="cbc-proj__sum"><div class="cbc-proj__pill" style="background:#b191cb;color:#ffffff;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.25);">Climate Change Adaptation</div><div class="cbc-proj__titleRow"><h4 class="cbc-proj__name">Sustainable Drainage Systems &amp; Greening the Grey - Edith Road</h4><div class="cbc-proj__right"><span class="cbc-proj__spent">£98,125.12</span><svg class="cbc-proj__chev" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path fill="currentColor" d="M5.3 7.3a1 1 0 0 1 1.4 0L10 10.6l3.3-3.3a1 1 0 1 1 1.4 1.4l-4 4a1 1 0 0 1-1.4 0l-4-4a1 1 0 0 1 0-1.4z"></path></svg></div></div></summary><div class="cbc-proj__body"><p>Rainwater gardens implemented at key locations along Edith Road to tackle the issue of surface water flooding as well as introduce greening along the streetscape to provide environmental and social benefits to residents.</p></div></details><details class="cbc-proj"><summary class="cbc-proj__sum"><div class="cbc-proj__pill" style="background:#b191cb;color:#ffffff;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.25);">Climate Change Adaptation</div><div class="cbc-proj__titleRow"><h4 class="cbc-proj__name">Sustainable Drainage Systems &amp; Greening the Grey - Eel Brook Common</h4><div class="cbc-proj__right"><span class="cbc-proj__spent">£80,000.00</span><svg class="cbc-proj__chev" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path fill="currentColor" d="M5.3 7.3a1 1 0 0 1 1.4 0L10 10.6l3.3-3.3a1 1 0 1 1 1.4 1.4l-4 4a1 1 0 0 1-1.4 0l-4-4a1 1 0 0 1 0-1.4z"></path></svg></div></div></summary><div class="cbc-proj__body"><p>Eel Brook Common transformed from a concrete eyesore into a vibrant green oasis. More than 1,800 square meters of concrete slabs removed and replaced with grass and wildflowers at the former paddling pool and play area near Effie Road (once a hotspot for anti-social behaviour).</p><p>Local volunteers came together in April 2024 to sow grass and plant colourful wildflowers, primroses, violets, and agrimony, boosting biodiversity in the area.</p><p>Funding supplemented by a £75,000 grant from the Mayor of London</p></div></details></div></section></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></section><div class="bg-colour--primary-surface bg-mask bg-mask--t-convex ai-scope"></div><section class="home-green-investing position-relative p-y-spacer-xs bg-colour--primary-surface ai-past-wrap ai-scope"><div class="container"><div class="row"><div class="col-12"><div id="ai-past-investments"><div class="flex-center"><h2 class="text-center m-b-spacer-sm">Investment history</h2></div><div class="flex-center"><div class="ai-past-table-choke"><table class="brand-table"><caption>Investment history</caption><thead><tr><th class="brand-table__head" scope="col"><strong>Investment</strong></th><th class="brand-table__head" scope="col"><strong>Interest</strong></th><th class="brand-table__head" scope="col"><strong>Term</strong></th><th cla